“Any software can fail in production. The goal is not zero crashes, but quick detection, isolation, and recovery.

On the backend, we use PM2 or Docker to keep a live health check on our Node.js application. If the app crashes due to any runtime error, it is automatically restarted, so downtime is minimal.

For debugging and visibility, we use Winston for application-level error logging and Morgan to log API requests, which helps us identify which endpoint or service is causing the issue.

On the frontend, we use React Error Boundaries so that if a component crashes, the entire application does not break and the user sees a fallback UI instead.

We also integrate Sentry in React, which automatically captures runtime errors and notifies developers via email or Slack. Developers can then view detailed error information like stack traces and affected users on the Sentry dashboard website.

This approach ensures system stability, good user experience, and fast issue resolution.”



====>PM2 is an open-source process manager for Node.js applications.

✔ Not purchased
